     "year": 2026,
     "cves": [
      "CVE-2026-114938"
     ],
     "note": "Only on x86-64 CPUs with AVX-512 VBMI (Intel Ice Lake and later Xeons and some Core chips, AMD Zen 4 and later); ARM64 is not affected. Also affected: Oracle Java SE 8 Enterprise Performance Pack 8u511b33-perf (fixed in 8u513-perf) and GraalVM Enterprise Edition 21.3.20.0.3. Interim mitigations (either one): -XX:-UseBASE64Intrinsics (preferred; VulnCheck tested it with -XX:+UnlockDiagnosticVMOptions ahead of it), or -XX:UseAVX=2 on x86-64 hosts only, since JVMs on ARM64 fail to start with it. A proof of concept that triggers the bug is public, and probing and exploit attempts have been seen since 18 November (GreyNoise, watchTowr); no confirmed compromise and not in CISA KEV as of 2026-11-19.",
